  "facts": [
    "The Lytle Tunnel, Ohio's longest vehicular tunnel at 335 meters, opened in 1970 and uniquely features three tubes: a two-lane southbound, a three-lane northbound, and a single-lane southbound exit ramp.",
    "Between 2001 and 2003, the Lytle Tunnel earned notoriety for truck accidents caused by drivers ignoring 40‑mph signs and a sharp curve, prompting OhioDOT to install radar speed signs in May 2003.",
    "During its construction, historic Lytle Park buildings were razed, yet the park was later rebuilt over the tunnel, becoming the first U.S. park constructed atop an interstate highway."
